    "answer": {
      "short": "$2$\n\nRationalise the denominator and cancel the common factor $x-1$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\lim_{x\\to1}\\frac{x-1}{\\sqrt{x}-1}&=\\lim_{x\\to1}\\frac{(x-1)(\\sqrt{x}+1)}{(\\sqrt{x}-1)(\\sqrt{x}+1)}\\\\\\lim_{x\\to1}\\frac{x-1}{\\sqrt{x}-1}&=\\lim_{x\\to1}\\frac{(x-1)(\\sqrt{x}+1)}{x-1}\\\\\\lim_{x\\to1}\\frac{x-1}{\\sqrt{x}-1}&=\\lim_{x\\to1}(\\sqrt{x}+1)\\\\\\lim_{x\\to1}\\frac{x-1}{\\sqrt{x}-1}&=\\sqrt{1}+1\\\\\\lim_{x\\to1}\\frac{x-1}{\\sqrt{x}-1}&=2\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
